==Trivia==
*The ン・トーベ ''N Tōbe'' part of Bento Region's Japanese name (ン・トーベ地方 ''N Tōbe Chihō'', "N Tōbe Region") is derived from 弁当 ''[[wikipedia:Bento|bentō]]''. All of the stages' Japanese names are related to ''bentō'', though the first two do not necessarily refer to food:
**The バラン ''Baran'' in [[Plastic Pastures]]' Japanese name (バラバラバラン草原 ''Barabara Baran Sōgen'', "Scattered Baran Grassland") refers to ''[[wikipedia:ja:人造バラン|jinzō baran]]'' (人造バラン), the [https://sushiuniversity.jp/basicknowledge/what-is-the-green-jagged-sheet-placed-in-between-sushi-and-sashimi green, jagged sheet] placed in between sushi and sashimi.
**The 橋 ''Hashi'' (Bridge) in [[Bridge of Forgotten Sporks]]' Japanese name (忘れられた橋 ''Wasurerareta Hashi'', "Forgotten Bridge") shares its pronunciation with 箸 (chopstick).

